2026-10-28T17:38:56.2985692Z {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013ML4aEkpk45t22eEqgcUs4","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t{\n2\t  \"number\": 21,\n3\t  \"url\": \"https://github.com/wzinl/cs467-as3-triage-agent/issues/21\",\n4\t  \"repo\": \"wzinl/cs467-as3-triage-agent\",\n5\t  \"title\": \"[Enhancement] Allow searching for aws_secretsmanager_secret via tag values\",\n6\t  \"body\": \"### Description\\n\\nThe current aws_secretsmanager_secret data source requires specifying a name or ARN of the secret.\\n\\nPlease add the ability to use tags to find the secret instead like other data sources do (e.x. `aws_lb`, `aws_subnet`, and `aws_instance`)\\n\\nI see some sources use the `tags` configuration for lookup while others use `filter` blocks. I would prefer the `tags` method but I'm not sure the standard being used going forward.\\n\\n### Affected Resource(s) or Data Source(s)\\n\\n* `data.aws_secretsmanager_secret`\\n\\n### Potential Terraform Configuration\\n\\n```hcl\\ndata \\\"aws_secretsmanager_secret\\\" \\\"ExampleLogin\\\" {\\n  tags = {\\n    CredentialsFor = \\\"auth.example.com\\\"\\n  }\\n}\\n```\\n\\n\\n### References\\n\\nhttps://docs.aws.amazon.com/secretsmanager/latest/apireference/API_ListSecrets.html#API_ListSecrets_RequestParameters\\n\\nAPI uses `filters` for tags\\n\\n### Would you like to implement the enhancement?\\n\\nNo\\n\",\n7\t  \"author\": \"zzzinn\",\n8\t  \"author_association\": \"NONE\",\n9\t  \"labels\": [\n10\t    \"enhancement\"\n11\t  ],\n12\t  \"created_at\": \"2026-10-28T17:08:53Z\",\n13\t  \"as_of\": \"2026-06-22T19:14:55Z\"\n14\t}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"96a343c0-5946-4444-8aae-fc6adca7306b","uuid":"7f3ca966-85d5-481c-9f93-ddd1322e2e25","timestamp":"2026-10-28T17:38:56.294Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/tmp/gh-aw/agent/issue.json","content":"{\n  \"number\": 21,\n  \"url\": \"https://github.com/wzinl/cs467-as3-triage-agent/issues/21\",\n  \"repo\": \"wzinl/cs467-as3-triage-agent\",\n  \"title\": \"[Enhancement] Allow searching for aws_secretsmanager_secret via tag values\",\n  \"body\": \"### Description\\n\\nThe current aws_secretsmanager_secret data source requires specifying a name or ARN of the secret.\\n\\nPlease add the ability to use tags to find the secret instead like other data sources do (e.x. `aws_lb`, `aws_subnet`, and `aws_instance`)\\n\\nI see some sources use the `tags` configuration for lookup while others use `filter` blocks. I would prefer the `tags` method but I'm not sure the standard being used going forward.\\n\\n### Affected Resource(s) or Data Source(s)\\n\\n* `data.aws_secretsmanager_secret`\\n\\n### Potential Terraform Configuration\\n\\n```hcl\\ndata \\\"aws_secretsmanager_secret\\\" \\\"ExampleLogin\\\" {\\n  tags = {\\n    CredentialsFor = \\\"auth.example.com\\\"\\n  }\\n}\\n```\\n\\n\\n### References\\n\\nhttps://docs.aws.amazon.com/secretsmanager/latest/apireference/API_ListSecrets.html#API_ListSecrets_RequestParameters\\n\\nAPI uses `filters` for tags\\n\\n### Would you like to implement the enhancement?\\n\\nNo\\n\",\n  \"author\": \"zzzinn\",\n  \"author_association\": \"NONE\",\n  \"labels\": [\n    \"enhancement\"\n  ],\n  \"created_at\": \"2026-10-28T17:08:53Z\",\n  \"as_of\": \"2026-06-22T19:14:55Z\"\n}","numLines":14,"startLine":1,"totalLines":14}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_013ML4aEkpk45t22eEqgcUs4","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
